    {
      "criterion": "Saving sends the full model array to `PUT /api/models` and handles 409 (referenced model deletion) by displaying the error with a message directing to the Replace Model feature",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "\"Load Defaults\" shows a confirmation dialog, calls the API, and displays slug-collision conflicts if returned",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The `cc_model` field includes helper text explaining its purpose",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T15:21:57Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T15:28:02Z",
      "duration_ms": 365000,
      "summary": [
        "Replaced the Model Registry tab stub with a full implementation in mcp-server/gui/public/views/config.js. The tab maintains module-level state (mrModels / mrOriginal / mrEditingId) initialized from server data on first render. Features implemented: model table with name/slug/cc_model columns; inline row editing with Edit/Done/Cancel buttons; dirty indicator dots on changed fields (compared against the original server snapshot); strikethrough + Restore button for pending deletions (no immediate DOM removal); client-side slug validation against /^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$/ with reserved 'inherit' check and inline error messages; Save button disabled while validation errors exist; Add Model form with auto-slug derivation from name (tracks whether slug has been manually overridden), editable slug field, cc_model field with helper text, and crypto.randomUUID() for new model IDs; Save (PUT /api/models) with 409 conflict handling directing users to Replace Model on Persona Models tab; Load Defaults (POST /api/models/load-defaults) with confirmation dialog and slug-collision conflict display. Added corresponding CSS classes (.mr-dirty-dot, .mr-model-deleted, .mr-model-new, .mr-edit-row, .mr-field-error, .mr-error-text, .mr-add-section, .mr-action-bar) to styles.css. All 3523 existing tests pass; Node --check confirms no syntax errors."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/gui/public/views/config.js",
          "mcp-server/gui/public/styles.css"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:28:02Z",
          "note": "mrRefreshDirtyDots() is a documented no-op stub. During inline editing, dirty dots are only updated on full re-renders (triggered by Done/Cancel/action buttons), not on every keystroke. This means a dirty dot won't appear while a user is mid-edit until they press Done. A future improvement could update the dot in real-time during input events without a full re-render, e.g. by toggling a CSS class on the <td> directly."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:28:02Z",
          "note": "The mrHasChanges() comparison in config.js uses index-based positional matching (mrModels[i] vs mrOriginal[i]) rather than ID-based matching. This is correct for the current bulk-save pattern where array order is stable, but would produce false positives if array reordering were ever added. A future refactor could switch to ID-keyed comparison."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:28:02Z",
          "note": "The Add Model form's slug auto-derivation tracks 'previous value' via a custom property on the DOM input element (addNameInput._prevValue). This is a pragmatic workaround to avoid full re-renders on every keystroke, but it couples logic to DOM state. If the Add form were ever extracted into a component, this pattern would need to be replaced with explicit state tracking."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T15:28:27Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T15:33:22Z",
      "duration_ms": 295000,
      "summary": [
        "All 9 acceptance criteria verified via static code analysis of config.js and styles.css. Node --check syntax validation passes. Full test suite runs clean: 3523 tests across 117 files pass with 0 failures, including 49 model-registry.test.ts and 36 api-models.test.ts targeted tests. All server-layer interactions (409 CONFLICT mapping, API.saveModels, API.loadDefaultModels) verified against api-models.ts and server.ts. Edge-case analysis: unsaved-changes guard correctly fires on tab navigation; state resets cleanly on page reload; empty-model-list, null-mrModels, and missing-response-key paths are all defensively handled. One low-priority observation noted regarding no unit tests for frontend helper functions (mrDeriveSlug, mrValidateSlug, mrHasChanges)."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "117 test files",
        "tests_passed": 3523,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "coverage-gap",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:33:22Z",
          "note": "The frontend helper functions mrDeriveSlug(), mrValidateSlug(), mrHasChanges(), and mrBuildTabHtml() in config.js have no dedicated unit tests. All are exercised indirectly via static code review and the backend api-models.test.ts suite (which covers the server-side equivalents). A future improvement could add a browser-environment (jsdom) test file that exercises these helpers directly, particularly the slug auto-derivation and dirty-comparison edge cases."
        },
        {
          "type": "edge-case",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:33:22Z",
          "note": "In-progress inline edits (typing in Edit row before clicking Done) are NOT reflected in configDirty.modelRegistry until Done is clicked. If a user switches tabs after editing a field but before clicking Done, those field edits are silently discarded without the unsaved-changes guard firing. The guard correctly fires for previously Done'd changes. This is an acceptable UX limitation — mid-edit field values are transient state, not committed to mrModels yet. Not an AC violation."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:33:22Z",
          "note": "The 409 conflict error message in mrDoSave() references 'Replace Model' but the Persona Models tab is currently a stub ('Coming soon'). When the Persona Models tab is implemented (likely a future WP), the error message wording is already correct and will naturally become actionable."
        }
      ]
